      "explanation": "'Загадать желание' means 'to make a wish' and is a beloved Russian New Year tradition -- you make a wish while the Kremlin clock chimes at midnight. 'Загадать' is perfective of 'загадывать'. The noun 'желание' (wish) comes from 'желать' (to wish). Example: 'Я загадала желание, когда куранты били' (I made a wish when the clock chimed).",
